    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, city-aware `postcode` validation for owner creation, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and keeping structural impact low by adding small, single-method units rather than growing existing classes.\n\n**New behaviour (one cohesive step + its handler):**\n- `ValidatePostcode.java` \u2014 a new single-method function inserted into the `POST /api/owners` pipeline. When a postcode is present it must be 4 digits and, for a city with a known region, fall in range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit value; absent postcode is skipped. Invalid ones throw a checked exception.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` + escalation YAML \u2014 respond `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`, mirroring the existing email/telephone validators.\n\n**Wiring & persistence (minimal edits):**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `validatePostcode` step between address normalization and the duplicate checks.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields`, so the generated request/response DTOs carry it (keeping the request contract backward-compatible).\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `postcode` column field plus getter/setter; MapStruct maps it by name on the way in and out with no mapper changes.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column; `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 added the matching `NULL` to each positional seed insert (required because those inserts omit a column list).\n\nThe region range check is enforced per the spec even though the tests only exercise the malformed and unknown-city cases.\n\nNote: I only wired postcode into the create (POST) pipeline since that is what the spec and tests cover; the PUT/update pipeline's `ApplyOwner` was intentionally left untouched to keep the change scoped.",
